<Base title="GATE beginner guide" description="Start GATE 2027 from zero: pick a paper, use the syllabus, build fundamentals, practice and revise — without coaching." canonicalPath="/guides/beginner/">
  <section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="kicker">Start here</p><h1>Beginner guide: start GATE from zero</h1><p class="lead">You need minimum prerequisites, one paper, one syllabus PDF, one resource per subject, and a daily practice habit. Not twenty books.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap grid cols-2">
    <div class="card"><h3>Week 1–2: orientation</h3><ol><li>Read the <a href="/gate-2027/">GATE 2027 hub</a> and <a href="/gate-2027/eligibility/">eligibility</a>.</li><li>Pick ONE paper (<a href="/gate-2027/papers/">directory</a>).</li><li>Download its 2027 syllabus PDF.</li><li>List subjects; rate confidence 1–5.</li><li>Build a plan in the <a href="/tools/study-planner/">study planner</a>.</li></ol></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Then: one topic at a time</h3><ol><li>Learn the minimum prerequisite only.</li><li>Study concept → simple example → GATE-level example.</li><li>Do 5–10 practice questions (<a href="/practice/">practice</a>).</li><li>Log misses in the <a href="/tools/mistake-tracker/">mistake tracker</a>.</li><li>Schedule revision (<a href="/tools/revision-planner/">revision planner</a>).</li></ol></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="card"><h3>What not to do</h3><ul><li>Don't collect 40 PDFs. Start with 1 primary + 1 practice + 1 backup per subject (<a href="/resources/">resources</a>).</li><li>Don't jump between papers.</li><li>Don't skip General Aptitude — it is common to all papers.</li><li>Don't buy a course before trying free fundamentals for 3 weeks.</li></ul></div></div></section>
</Base>
